WEBVTT

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.072
One dollar and eighty-seven cents.

00:00:18.072 --> 00:00:19.896
That was all.

00:00:19.896 --> 00:00:22.992
And sixty cents of it was in pennies.

00:00:22.992 --> 00:00:26.208
Pennies saved one and two at a time

00:00:26.208 --> 00:00:30.264
by bulldozing the grocer and the vegetable man and the butcher

00:00:30.264 --> 00:00:34.824
until one’s cheeks burned with the silent imputation of parsimony

00:00:34.824 --> 00:00:37.704
that such close dealing implied.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:40.392
Three times Della counted it.

00:00:40.392 --> 00:00:43.464
One dollar and eighty-seven cents.

00:00:43.464 --> 00:00:46.248
And the next day would be Christmas.

00:00:46.248 --> 00:00:48.984
There was clearly nothing to do

00:00:48.984 --> 00:00:52.704
but flop down on the shabby little couch and howl.

00:00:52.704 --> 00:00:54.672
So Della did it.

00:00:54.672 --> 00:00:57.744
Which instigates the moral reflection

00:00:57.744 --> 00:01:02.424
that life is made up of sobs, sniffles, and smiles,

00:01:02.424 --> 00:01:05.040
with sniffles predominating.

00:01:05.042 --> 00:01:10.298
While the mistress of the home is gradually subsiding from the first stage to the second,

00:01:10.298 --> 00:01:12.554
take a look at the home.

00:01:12.554 --> 00:01:15.746
A furnished flat at $8 per week.

00:01:15.746 --> 00:01:18.818
It did not exactly beggar description,

00:01:18.818 --> 00:01:23.282
but it certainly had that word on the lookout for the mendicancy squad.

00:01:23.282 --> 00:01:27.842
In the vestibule below was a letter-box into which no letter would go,

00:01:27.842 --> 00:01:32.474
and an electric button from which no mortal finger could coax a ring.

00:01:32.474 --> 00:01:36.626
Also appertaining thereunto was a card bearing the name

00:01:36.626 --> 00:01:39.290
“Mr. James Dillingham Young.”

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:42.338
The “Dillingham” had been flung to the breeze

00:01:42.338 --> 00:01:45.530
during a former period of prosperity

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:49.490
when its possessor was being paid $30 per week.

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:53.642
Now, when the income was shrunk to $20, though,

00:01:53.642 --> 00:01:58.562
they were thinking seriously of contracting to a modest and unassuming D.

00:01:58.562 --> 00:02:03.698
But whenever Mr. James Dillingham Young came home and reached his flat above

00:02:03.698 --> 00:02:08.474
he was called “Jim” and greatly hugged by Mrs. James Dillingham Young,

00:02:08.474 --> 00:02:11.402
already introduced to you as Della.

00:02:11.402 --> 00:02:13.802
Which is all very good.

00:02:13.792 --> 00:02:18.184
Della finished her cry and attended to her cheeks with the powder rag.

00:02:18.184 --> 00:02:21.472
She stood by the window and looked out dully

00:02:21.472 --> 00:02:25.696
at a gray cat walking a gray fence in a gray backyard.

00:02:25.696 --> 00:02:28.384
Tomorrow would be Christmas Day,

00:02:28.384 --> 00:02:33.520
and she had only $1.87 with which to buy Jim a present.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:38.152
She had been saving every penny she could for months, with this result.

00:02:38.152 --> 00:02:41.248
Twenty dollars a week doesn’t go far.

00:02:41.248 --> 00:02:45.016
Expenses had been greater than she had calculated.

00:02:45.016 --> 00:02:46.960
They always are.

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:52.936
Only $1.87 to buy a present for Jim. Her Jim.

00:02:52.936 --> 00:02:57.424
Many a happy hour she had spent planning for something nice for him.

00:02:57.424 --> 00:03:00.712
Something fine and rare and sterling—

00:03:00.712 --> 00:03:04.552
something just a little bit near to being worthy of the honor

00:03:04.552 --> 00:03:07.024
of being owned by Jim.

00:03:07.024 --> 00:03:10.744
There was a pier glass between the windows of the room.

00:03:10.744 --> 00:03:14.608
Perhaps you have seen a pier glass in an $8 flat.

00:03:14.608 --> 00:03:18.160
A very thin and very agile person may,

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:23.200
by observing his reflection in a rapid sequence of longitudinal strips,

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:26.848
obtain a fairly accurate conception of his looks.

00:03:26.848 --> 00:03:30.664
Della, being slender, had mastered the art.

00:03:30.664 --> 00:03:35.128
Suddenly she whirled from the window and stood before the glass.

00:03:35.128 --> 00:03:37.936
Her eyes were shining brilliantly,

00:03:37.936 --> 00:03:42.064
but her face had lost its color within twenty seconds.

00:03:42.064 --> 00:03:44.992
Rapidly she pulled down her hair

00:03:44.992 --> 00:03:47.872
and let it fall to its full length.

00:03:47.875 --> 00:03:52.267
Now, there were two possessions of the James Dillingham Youngs

00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:55.363
in which they both took a mighty pride.

00:03:55.363 --> 00:04:00.187
One was Jim’s gold watch that had been his father’s and his grandfather’s.

00:04:00.187 --> 00:04:02.539
The other was Della’s hair.

00:04:02.539 --> 00:04:06.595
Had the queen of Sheba lived in the flat across the airshaft,

00:04:06.595 --> 00:04:10.795
Della would have let her hair hang out the window some day to dry

00:04:10.795 --> 00:04:14.851
just to depreciate Her Majesty’s jewels and gifts.

00:04:14.851 --> 00:04:17.731
Had King Solomon been the janitor,

00:04:17.731 --> 00:04:21.067
with all his treasures piled up in the basement,

00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:24.907
Jim would have pulled out his watch every time he passed,

00:04:24.907 --> 00:04:28.147
just to see him pluck at his beard from envy.

00:04:28.147 --> 00:04:31.627
So now Della’s beautiful hair fell about her

00:04:31.627 --> 00:04:35.659
rippling and shining like a cascade of brown waters.

00:04:35.659 --> 00:04:38.035
It reached below her knee

00:04:38.035 --> 00:04:41.275
and made itself almost a garment for her.

00:04:41.275 --> 00:04:44.659
And then she did it up again nervously and quickly.

00:04:44.659 --> 00:04:47.971
Once she faltered for a minute and stood still

00:04:47.971 --> 00:04:51.955
while a tear or two splashed on the worn red carpet.

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:56.350
On went her old brown jacket; on went her old brown hat.

00:04:56.350 --> 00:05:00.862
With a whirl of skirts and with the brilliant sparkle still in her eyes,

00:05:00.862 --> 00:05:04.750
she fluttered out the door and down the stairs to the street.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:07.462
Where she stopped the sign read:

00:05:07.462 --> 00:05:11.950
“Mme. Sofronie. Hair Goods of All Kinds.”

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:16.870
One flight up Della ran, and collected herself, panting.

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:22.534
Madame, large, too white, chilly, hardly looked the “Sofronie.”

00:05:22.534 --> 00:05:25.534
“Will you buy my hair?” asked Della.

00:05:25.534 --> 00:05:28.222
“I buy hair,” said Madame.

00:05:28.222 --> 00:05:31.966
“Take yer hat off and let’s have a sight at the looks of it.”

00:05:31.966 --> 00:05:34.870
Down rippled the brown cascade.

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:39.934
“Twenty dollars,” said Madame, lifting the mass with a practised hand.

00:05:39.934 --> 00:05:42.814
“Give it to me quick,” said Della.

00:05:42.833 --> 00:05:46.985
Oh, and the next two hours tripped by on rosy wings.

00:05:46.985 --> 00:05:49.457
Forget the hashed metaphor.

00:05:49.457 --> 00:05:53.129
She was ransacking the stores for Jim’s present.

00:05:53.129 --> 00:05:55.505
She found it at last.

00:05:55.505 --> 00:05:59.177
It surely had been made for Jim and no one else.

00:05:59.177 --> 00:06:02.609
There was no other like it in any of the stores,

00:06:02.609 --> 00:06:05.825
and she had turned all of them inside out.

00:06:05.825 --> 00:06:10.025
It was a platinum fob chain simple and chaste in design,

00:06:10.025 --> 00:06:13.985
properly proclaiming its value by substance alone

00:06:13.985 --> 00:06:17.297
and not by meretricious ornamentation—

00:06:17.297 --> 00:06:19.817
as all good things should do.

00:06:19.817 --> 00:06:22.577
It was even worthy of The Watch.

00:06:22.577 --> 00:06:26.345
As soon as she saw it she knew that it must be Jim’s.

00:06:26.345 --> 00:06:28.337
It was like him.

00:06:28.337 --> 00:06:32.489
Quietness and value—the description applied to both.

00:06:32.489 --> 00:06:35.705
Twenty-one dollars they took from her for it,

00:06:35.705 --> 00:06:39.233
and she hurried home with the 87 cents.

00:06:39.233 --> 00:06:41.849
With that chain on his watch

00:06:41.849 --> 00:06:45.785
Jim might be properly anxious about the time in any company.

00:06:45.785 --> 00:06:48.089
Grand as the watch was,

00:06:48.089 --> 00:06:51.065
he sometimes looked at it on the sly

00:06:51.065 --> 00:06:55.433
on account of the old leather strap that he used in place of a chain.

00:06:55.417 --> 00:06:57.769
When Della reached home

00:06:57.769 --> 00:07:01.921
her intoxication gave way a little to prudence and reason.

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:05.713
She got out her curling irons and lighted the gas

00:07:05.713 --> 00:07:10.681
and went to work repairing the ravages made by generosity added to love.

00:07:10.681 --> 00:07:14.665
Which is always a tremendous task, dear friends—

00:07:14.665 --> 00:07:16.777
a mammoth task.

00:07:16.777 --> 00:07:22.081
Within forty minutes her head was covered with tiny, close-lying curls

00:07:22.081 --> 00:07:25.801
that made her look wonderfully like a truant schoolboy.

00:07:25.801 --> 00:07:28.705
She looked at her reflection in the mirror

00:07:28.705 --> 00:07:32.089
long, carefully, and critically.

00:07:32.089 --> 00:07:35.641
“If Jim doesn’t kill me,” she said to herself,

00:07:35.641 --> 00:07:38.569
“before he takes a second look at me,

00:07:38.569 --> 00:07:42.505
he’ll say I look like a Coney Island chorus girl.

00:07:42.505 --> 00:07:45.121
But what could I do—oh!

00:07:45.121 --> 00:07:48.793
what could I do with a dollar and eighty-seven cents?”

00:07:48.792 --> 00:07:51.816
At 7 o’clock the coffee was made

00:07:51.816 --> 00:07:55.200
and the frying-pan was on the back of the stove

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:58.008
hot and ready to cook the chops.

00:07:58.008 --> 00:08:00.288
Jim was never late.

00:08:00.288 --> 00:08:03.456
Della doubled the fob chain in her hand

00:08:03.456 --> 00:08:07.824
and sat on the corner of the table near the door that he always entered.

00:08:07.824 --> 00:08:12.192
Then she heard his step on the stair away down on the first flight,

00:08:12.192 --> 00:08:15.120
and she turned white for just a moment.

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:18.744
She had a habit of saying a little silent prayer

00:08:18.744 --> 00:08:21.672
about the simplest everyday things,

00:08:21.672 --> 00:08:23.928
and now she whispered:

00:08:23.928 --> 00:08:27.384
“Please God, make him think I am still pretty.”

00:08:27.384 --> 00:08:30.864
The door opened and Jim stepped in and closed it.

00:08:30.864 --> 00:08:33.864
He looked thin and very serious.

00:08:33.864 --> 00:08:37.176
Poor fellow, he was only twenty-two—

00:08:37.176 --> 00:08:39.960
and to be burdened with a family!

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:43.824
He needed a new overcoat and he was without gloves.

00:08:43.824 --> 00:08:46.488
Jim stopped inside the door,

00:08:46.488 --> 00:08:50.016
as immovable as a setter at the scent of quail,

00:08:50.016 --> 00:08:52.728
His eyes were fixed upon Della,

00:08:52.728 --> 00:08:56.376
and there was an expression in them that she could not read,

00:08:56.376 --> 00:08:58.608
and it terrified her.

00:08:58.608 --> 00:09:03.816
It was not anger, nor surprise, nor disapproval, nor horror,

00:09:03.816 --> 00:09:07.488
nor any of the sentiments that she had been prepared for.

00:09:07.488 --> 00:09:10.464
He simply stared at her fixedly

00:09:10.464 --> 00:09:13.920
with that peculiar expression on his face.

00:09:13.917 --> 00:09:17.157
Della wriggled off the table and went for him.

00:09:17.157 --> 00:09:21.573
“Jim, darling,” she cried, “don’t look at me that way.

00:09:21.573 --> 00:09:24.549
I had my hair cut off and sold

00:09:24.549 --> 00:09:27.693
because I couldn’t have lived through Christmas

00:09:27.693 --> 00:09:30.189
without giving you a present.

00:09:30.189 --> 00:09:33.741
It’ll grow out again—you won’t mind, will you?

00:09:33.741 --> 00:09:35.901
I just had to do it.

00:09:35.901 --> 00:09:38.733
My hair grows awfully fast.

00:09:38.733 --> 00:09:43.845
Say ‘Merry Christmas!’ Jim, and let’s be happy.

00:09:43.845 --> 00:09:46.269
You don’t know what a nice—

00:09:46.269 --> 00:09:49.893
what a beautiful, nice gift I’ve got for you.”

00:09:49.893 --> 00:09:54.045
“You’ve cut off your hair?” asked Jim, laboriously,

00:09:54.045 --> 00:09:57.669
as if he had not arrived at that patent fact yet

00:09:57.669 --> 00:10:00.693
even after the hardest mental labor.

00:10:00.693 --> 00:10:03.741
“Cut it off and sold it,” said Della.

00:10:03.741 --> 00:10:06.837
“Don’t you like me just as well, anyhow?

00:10:06.837 --> 00:10:09.741
I’m me without my hair, ain’t I?”

00:10:09.741 --> 00:10:12.741
Jim looked about the room curiously.

00:10:12.741 --> 00:10:16.101
“You say your hair is gone?” he said,

00:10:16.101 --> 00:10:18.789
with an air almost of idiocy.

00:10:18.789 --> 00:10:21.741
“You needn’t look for it,” said Della.

00:10:21.741 --> 00:10:25.797
“It’s sold, I tell you—sold and gone, too.

00:10:25.797 --> 00:10:31.389
It’s Christmas Eve, boy. Be good to me, for it went for you.

00:10:31.389 --> 00:10:36.765
Maybe the hairs of my head were numbered,” she went on with sudden serious sweetness,

00:10:36.765 --> 00:10:40.053
“but nobody could ever count my love for you.

00:10:40.053 --> 00:10:42.957
Shall I put the chops on, Jim?”

00:10:42.957 --> 00:10:46.413
Out of his trance Jim seemed quickly to wake.

00:10:46.413 --> 00:10:48.765
He enfolded his Della.

00:10:48.765 --> 00:10:52.701
For ten seconds let us regard with discreet scrutiny

00:10:52.701 --> 00:10:56.469
some inconsequential object in the other direction.

00:10:56.469 --> 00:10:59.613
Eight dollars a week or a million a year—

00:10:59.613 --> 00:11:01.821
what is the difference?

00:11:01.821 --> 00:11:05.637
A mathematician or a wit would give you the wrong answer.

00:11:05.637 --> 00:11:10.197
The magi brought valuable gifts, but that was not among them.

00:11:10.197 --> 00:11:13.989
This dark assertion will be illuminated later on.

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:17.456
Jim drew a package from his overcoat pocket

00:11:17.456 --> 00:11:19.976
and threw it upon the table.

00:11:19.976 --> 00:11:24.296
“Don’t make any mistake, Dell,” he said, “about me.

00:11:24.296 --> 00:11:28.904
I don’t think there’s anything in the way of a haircut or a shave or a shampoo

00:11:28.904 --> 00:11:32.096
that could make me like my girl any less.

00:11:32.096 --> 00:11:34.808
But if you’ll unwrap that package

00:11:34.808 --> 00:11:38.504
you may see why you had me going a while at first.”

00:11:38.504 --> 00:11:42.320
White fingers and nimble tore at the string and paper.

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:45.320
And then an ecstatic scream of joy;

00:11:45.320 --> 00:11:51.848
and then, alas! a quick feminine change to hysterical tears and wails,

00:11:51.848 --> 00:11:55.112
necessitating the immediate employment

00:11:55.112 --> 00:11:58.568
of all the comforting powers of the lord of the flat.

00:11:58.568 --> 00:12:03.104
For there lay The Combs—the set of combs, side and back,

00:12:03.104 --> 00:12:06.800
that Della had worshipped long in a Broadway window.

00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:11.528
Beautiful combs, pure tortoise shell, with jewelled rims—

00:12:11.528 --> 00:12:15.128
just the shade to wear in the beautiful vanished hair.

00:12:15.128 --> 00:12:18.416
They were expensive combs, she knew,

00:12:18.416 --> 00:12:22.136
and her heart had simply craved and yearned over them

00:12:22.136 --> 00:12:24.896
without the least hope of possession.

00:12:24.896 --> 00:12:27.656
And now, they were hers,

00:12:27.656 --> 00:12:31.856
but the tresses that should have adorned the coveted adornments were gone.

00:12:31.856 --> 00:12:34.400
But she hugged them to her bosom,

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:39.032
and at length she was able to look up with dim eyes and a smile and say:

00:12:39.032 --> 00:12:42.368
“My hair grows so fast, Jim!”

00:12:42.368 --> 00:12:47.432
And then Della leaped up like a little singed cat and cried, “Oh, oh!”

00:12:47.417 --> 00:12:50.897
Jim had not yet seen his beautiful present.

00:12:50.897 --> 00:12:54.761
She held it out to him eagerly upon her open palm.

00:12:54.761 --> 00:12:57.929
The dull precious metal seemed to flash

00:12:57.929 --> 00:13:01.361
with a reflection of her bright and ardent spirit.

00:13:01.361 --> 00:13:04.097
“Isn’t it a dandy, Jim?

00:13:04.097 --> 00:13:07.145
I hunted all over town to find it.

00:13:07.145 --> 00:13:10.865
You’ll have to look at the time a hundred times a day now.

00:13:10.865 --> 00:13:12.929
Give me your watch.

00:13:12.929 --> 00:13:15.617
I want to see how it looks on it.”

00:13:15.617 --> 00:13:19.601
Instead of obeying, Jim tumbled down on the couch

00:13:19.601 --> 00:13:23.489
and put his hands under the back of his head and smiled.

00:13:23.489 --> 00:13:27.785
“Dell,” said he, “let’s put our Christmas presents away

00:13:27.785 --> 00:13:30.233
and keep ’em a while.

00:13:30.233 --> 00:13:33.473
They’re too nice to use just at present.

00:13:33.473 --> 00:13:37.145
I sold the watch to get the money to buy your combs.

00:13:37.145 --> 00:13:40.169
And now suppose you put the chops on.”

00:13:40.167 --> 00:13:45.399
The magi, as you know, were wise men—wonderfully wise men—

00:13:45.399 --> 00:13:48.543
who brought gifts to the Babe in the manger.

00:13:48.543 --> 00:13:52.047
They invented the art of giving Christmas presents.

00:13:52.047 --> 00:13:56.199
Being wise, their gifts were no doubt wise ones,

00:13:56.199 --> 00:14:00.567
possibly bearing the privilege of exchange in case of duplication.

00:14:00.567 --> 00:14:03.735
And here I have lamely related to you

00:14:03.735 --> 00:14:08.055
the uneventful chronicle of two foolish children in a flat

00:14:08.055 --> 00:14:11.631
who most unwisely sacrificed for each other

00:14:11.631 --> 00:14:14.559
the greatest treasures of their house.

00:14:14.559 --> 00:14:18.039
But in a last word to the wise of these days

00:14:18.039 --> 00:14:21.279
let it be said that of all who give gifts

00:14:21.279 --> 00:14:23.943
these two were the wisest.

00:14:23.943 --> 00:14:28.263
Of all who give and receive gifts, such as they are wisest.

00:14:28.263 --> 00:14:30.807
Everywhere they are wisest.

00:14:30.807 --> 00:14:32.871
They are the magi.
